WEBVTT

1
00:00:17.181 --> 00:00:20.743
Hermes dabbed his mouth with a cloth and stood up from the dinner table.

2
00:00:21.763 --> 00:00:23.484
He glanced at Markos and Julia.

3
00:00:23.504 --> 00:00:27.827
"Too bad Markos and the girl forgot to get more eels, though.

4
00:00:28.607 --> 00:00:29.988
I would have liked a third helping."

5
00:00:31.324 --> 00:00:35.126
"I'm so sorry, Hermes," Markos' father, Nikolaos, said.

6
00:00:35.146 --> 00:00:37.788
"I thought we had plenty of eels.

7
00:00:38.248 --> 00:00:39.288
It won't happen again."

8
00:00:39.308 --> 00:00:43.131
"Come, my friend," Caerus told Hermes.

9
00:00:43.791 --> 00:00:46.673
"Let's find Dionysus and celebrate the fine evening."

10
00:00:46.693 --> 00:00:50.655
"Yes." Hermes shot Brody a frown.

11
00:00:50.675 --> 00:00:56.278
"Although I'm not much in the mood for celebrating after today's chariot practice."

12
00:00:57.378 --> 00:01:00.020
Without another word the two gods left.

13
00:01:01.192 --> 00:01:05.954
Nikolaos frowned at his wife, who was helping Julia and the other girls clear the dishes.

14
00:01:05.974 --> 00:01:09.556
"That was an embarrassment," he said.

15
00:01:09.576 --> 00:01:12.737
"You know that eels are Hermes' favorite!"

16
00:01:14.038 --> 00:01:16.939
"How could I predict he'd eat twice as many as usual?"

17
00:01:17.399 --> 00:01:19.380
his wife retorted, sounding grumpy.

18
00:01:20.321 --> 00:01:22.001
She snapped her fingers at Markos.

19
00:01:23.322 --> 00:01:27.984
"Markos! Go to the agora right now and tell the vendor that we'll want more eels this week.

20
00:01:28.864 --> 00:01:31.987
We want only the freshest ones and plenty of them!"

21
00:01:33.328 --> 00:01:34.008
"Yes, Mother."

22
00:01:34.509 --> 00:01:35.369
Markos stood up.

23
00:01:37.091 --> 00:01:39.713
"We'll come along and help you, Markos," Julia said.

24
00:01:39.733 --> 00:01:40.934
"Right, Brody?"

25
00:01:40.954 --> 00:01:44.477
"Huh?" Brody looked up from his meal.

26
00:01:44.497 --> 00:01:46.038
"I'm not finished eating."

27
00:01:46.058 --> 00:01:54.325
"Come on," Julia said, yanking on his chiton so hard that Brody was afraid she was going to

28
00:01:54.385 --> 00:01:55.226
pull it right off.

29
00:01:56.767 --> 00:01:57.608
He glared at her.

30
00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:01.221
Back home he had barely noticed that Julia existed.

31
00:02:02.921 --> 00:02:07.283
She was just a nerd who never came to the football games or did anything else interesting.

32
00:02:08.483 --> 00:02:11.544
It was a lot harder to ignore her here in ancient Greece.

33
00:02:12.224 --> 00:02:13.985
When had she become so assertive?

34
00:02:15.145 --> 00:02:16.845
He sighed loudly and stood up.

35
00:02:16.865 --> 00:02:20.266
"Fine," he said.

36
00:02:20.286 --> 00:02:25.908
"I'm exhausted after my long day of training for the Olympics, but whatever."

37
00:02:28.148 --> 00:02:31.130
He grabbed one last olive and tossed it into his mouth.

38
00:02:33.731 --> 00:02:36.553
Soon the three of them were walking toward the agora.

39
00:02:36.573 --> 00:02:39.154
"What do you think?"

40
00:02:39.634 --> 00:02:40.895
Julia asked Markos.

41
00:02:40.915 --> 00:02:46.658
"Is there any chance that Brody will get good enough at chariot racing in time to win at

42
00:02:46.698 --> 00:02:47.238
the Games?"

43
00:02:47.258 --> 00:02:49.940
"Why don't you ask me?"

44
00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:51.120
Brody said.

45
00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:53.482
"I'm the one who has to do it.

46
00:02:53.762 --> 00:02:57.404
And controlling a bunch of crazy wild horses isn't as easy as it looks."

47
00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:01.581
"It didn't look easy at all," Julia said.

48
00:03:01.601 --> 00:03:03.582
"That's exactly my point.

49
00:03:05.723 --> 00:03:07.564
What if you don't improve fast enough?

50
00:03:08.704 --> 00:03:12.206
If you don't impress Hermes, he might break his promise to let us leave."

51
00:03:13.927 --> 00:03:14.767
Brody shrugged.

52
00:03:14.787 --> 00:03:16.948
"I have more than a week to practice.

53
00:03:17.328 --> 00:03:19.829
Besides, who cares what Hermes thinks of me right now?

54
00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:25.632
If I look bad at chariot driving, he'll be even more impressed when I win on the big

55
00:03:25.692 --> 00:03:29.221
day!" Julia still looked worried.

56
00:03:29.241 --> 00:03:32.723
"I don't want to get stuck here in ancient Greece forever."

57
00:03:34.724 --> 00:03:36.225
She glanced over at Markos.

58
00:03:36.245 --> 00:03:38.186
"Sorry, Markos.

59
00:03:38.486 --> 00:03:39.447
I don't mean to offend you."

60
00:03:39.467 --> 00:03:43.609
"Don't worry, I'll win," Brody said.

61
00:03:43.629 --> 00:03:44.950
"End of story."

62
00:03:46.331 --> 00:03:48.392
By then they were entering the agora.

63
00:03:49.032 --> 00:03:52.094
Several young men were gathered near a fabric vendor's stall.

64
00:03:53.294 --> 00:03:55.816
Brody recognized most of them as other champions.

65
00:03:57.116 --> 00:03:58.117
A few waved to him.

66
00:03:58.137 --> 00:04:00.759
"Did you hear the news?"

67
00:04:01.219 --> 00:04:02.560
Apollo's champion called.

68
00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:04.641
"The mighty Alcides arrives soon."

69
00:04:06.183 --> 00:04:08.804
"We heard all about it," Brody replied.

70
00:04:08.824 --> 00:04:10.786
"So what?

71
00:04:11.086 --> 00:04:13.348
I'm glad we'll finally get the chance to see this guy."

72
00:04:14.508 --> 00:04:16.270
Artemis' champion shook his head.

73
00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:19.332
"I'm not so sure I want to see him," he said.

74
00:04:19.352 --> 00:04:25.096
"I overheard Artemis talking with Ares and Hestia, the goddess of the hearth and home.

75
00:04:26.192 --> 00:04:31.273
Zeus told them that Alcides strangled two enormous serpents with his bare hands when he was less than

76
00:04:31.293 --> 00:04:31.974
a year old!"

77
00:04:31.994 --> 00:04:37.095
"Serpents? That's nothing," said Demeter's champion.

78
00:04:37.115 --> 00:04:42.036
"I heard that Alcides killed a dozen men before he was ten years old!"

79
00:04:42.056 --> 00:04:48.838
"Well, I heard that Alcides eats human brains for breakfast," Artemis' champion added.

80
00:04:48.858 --> 00:04:51.659
"Zeus says it makes him smarter."

81
00:04:51.679 --> 00:04:55.540
"That makes sense," put in Ares' champion.

82
00:04:56.664 --> 00:05:00.666
"Because Ares told me that Alcides eats human muscles for lunch.

83
00:05:01.127 --> 00:05:02.587
It's supposed to make him stronger."

84
00:05:03.648 --> 00:05:07.950
Brody listened, not sure what to think about what the athletes were saying.

85
00:05:09.111 --> 00:05:11.732
All these rumors were getting pretty tiring though.

86
00:05:13.153 --> 00:05:17.876
Just then a sleek deer raced toward them, dodging around the people in the agora.

87
00:05:17.896 --> 00:05:21.097
"Whoa," Brody said.

88
00:05:21.117 --> 00:05:22.518
"Loose animal!"

89
00:05:23.879 --> 00:05:25.540
The deer stopped in front of the group.

90
00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:28.882
It seemed pretty tame, so Brody stepped toward it.

91
00:05:30.083 --> 00:05:34.025
He was about to grab the deer when it suddenly transformed into Artemis.

92
00:05:34.045 --> 00:05:37.748
"Whoa!" Brody said again.

93
00:05:38.368 --> 00:05:41.710
He couldn't get used to the way the gods could transform into animals!

94
00:05:43.071 --> 00:05:45.133
Artemis crooked her finger at her champion.

95
00:05:45.153 --> 00:05:47.855
"Come, my boy," she ordered.

96
00:05:47.875 --> 00:05:50.136
"You need to rest.

97
00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:52.758
We have much more training to do tomorrow."

98
00:05:52.778 --> 00:05:55.860
"Coming," her champion said.

99
00:05:57.732 --> 00:06:00.334
"I'd better go, too," one of the others said.

100
00:06:00.354 --> 00:06:02.836
"Ares will be looking for me."

101
00:06:05.498 --> 00:06:09.260
Before long Brody, Julia, and Markos were alone again.

102
00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:13.143
"Wow," Julia said.

103
00:06:13.163 --> 00:06:15.865
"This Alcides sounds really impressive.

104
00:06:16.365 --> 00:06:17.706
I'm surprised I've never heard of him.

105
00:06:19.408 --> 00:06:21.669
Though that story about the serpents seemed familiar.

106
00:06:21.689 --> 00:06:23.911
I think—" "You haven't heard of him?"

107
00:06:24.351 --> 00:06:25.392
Brody cut her off.

108
00:06:27.692 --> 00:06:28.252
"That's cool.

109
00:06:28.633 --> 00:06:31.074
It means Zeus is probably exaggerating, right?

110
00:06:32.595 --> 00:06:37.339
I mean, if Alcides was really that great, wouldn't we have studied him in social studies class?"

111
00:06:37.359 --> 00:06:41.442
"Maybe." Julia looked troubled.

112
00:06:41.462 --> 00:06:47.286
"Then again, it's not as if we could possibly learn everything about ancient Greece.

113
00:06:49.227 --> 00:06:54.371
Maybe Alcides really is a great hero, just not quite as great as the really famous ones like

114
00:06:54.671 --> 00:06:56.212
Heracles or Achilles."

115
00:06:57.776 --> 00:06:58.397
She sighed.

116
00:06:58.417 --> 00:07:02.639
"I wish I had my phone so I could look him up on the Internet."

117
00:07:04.321 --> 00:07:05.802
Markos looked uncomfortable.

118
00:07:07.042 --> 00:07:12.286
Brody had noticed that Markos looked that way whenever Brody and Julia discussed their lives in the future.

119
00:07:16.649 --> 00:07:18.450
getting dark," Markos said.

120
00:07:18.470 --> 00:07:21.472
"We should tell the vendor about the eels and get home.

121
00:07:22.913 --> 00:07:24.674
Brody, you need to rest too.

122
00:07:25.114 --> 00:07:27.156
Tomorrow is likely to be a busy day."
